# Port patch for retail data (EU discs; tester picture 31.10.2026, Spanish: the merchant's line for the handcannon,
# "Extranjero. ¿Para qué te hace falta semejante cosa?", ended about 34 units past the right edge of the text
# window). The European BuyItemNum::move (Sscrn.rel text 0x25700, read with retail_code.py and the module's
# relocations on 31.10.2026) puts the buy line at the window point itself: its buy_msg_x is 0 (the prototype's
# and the US release's 0x37; the variable is only read), it adds no buy_msg_y for messages 0xA / 0x13, and for
# every language but English (pSys->language != 1) it shows the line at once (attribute 0x40, no typing). The
# European texts are longer than the English ones. With the debug and US discs unchanged. layout_tbl (mes.cpp,
# European main.dol 0x801F8E04) differs only in Japanese rows: not the cause.
